A||||9||gomobile||Wipers come on by themsleves?||||6||
Z||000000||gomobile||09-04-2001||02:28 PM||||I have notice that lately the wipers come on by themselves when I start the car? Any ideas why? Note: It never use to.||||reg||6
Z||000001||Haagster||09-04-2001||02:32 PM||||Wash it recently?  If so, it'll stop when it dries out...||||reg||6
Z||000002||chester||09-04-2001||02:43 PM||||Seems to be common cause 2 out of 3 of our GT's do it as well.  Never really investigated to see why.<P>Rob D.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||09-04-2001||02:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gomobile:<BR><B>I have notice that lately the wipers come on by themselves when I start the car? Any ideas why? Note: It never use to.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you had done a search you would have found lots of threads on this.<P>Here is my findings on the <B>Phantom wiper swipe!</B><P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012332.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012332.html</A> <P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||09-04-2001||02:59 PM||||Bad parking cam inside.<BR>I have an 86 that does that, it get sort of anoying!||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||09-04-2001||07:29 PM||||also a bad, worn or shorted connection in the turn sig, cruise, wiper stalk.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroLisa||09-04-2001||08:46 PM||||When I start my wipers they are way erratic... WHen I turn them on, they won't do a full swipe until I jiggle the handle a bit, but then they won't turn off no matter what I do!...I hate it when it rains, cause they are a big pain in my butt!||||reg||1
Z||000007||ka4nkf||09-04-2001||10:30 PM||||I have done a lot of testing with this problem, and my findings is in the Intermittant section of the control board.<BR>The reason I say this I have not heard of a wiper problem with the non intermitting wiper.<BR>I have worked with the wiper board on mine and did a lot of replacing parts on it(resistors & such). I messed with mine so much and did something that I don't know what I did. Mine does not do any famton wipe any more but I only have high speed. This is fine with me because I don't have the start up wipe but still got windshield wipers. My sujestion is go to the boneyard and get another board out of one of the motors.||||reg||1
Z||000008||redfiero||09-05-2001||06:39 AM||||My wipers used to do the same thing.  I found that I had a bad ground in the front, passengers side turn signal.  The actual socket had the wire broken inside.  I fixed that, no more phantom wipers!<P>matt||||reg||7
Z||000009||Patrick86GT||09-05-2001||10:04 PM||||Paul, thanks for noting the thread. I've experienced the phantom problem in my 86Gt but was never annoyed enuff to really get after it.<P>being a "parts changer" (vs. mechanic), to repair the cruise, i replaced the stalk and expected it to solve 2 problems: non-functioning cruise & phantom wiper. the new (GM) stalk didn't fix either problem but the white lettering sure looks perfect! <P>I've printed out your comments and will be following thru w/ a wiper repair one of these days. And (I recall) Paul Vargas has a good cruise repair guide on his web site....so, THANKS, i can now fix both problems!<P>Pat<BR>||||reg||1
